        "numerical_bug": {
          "answer": {
            "is_numerical_bug": true,
            "category": "accuracy",
            "confidence": 0.9,
            "rationale": "The PR fixes a numerical issue in SVD for near-identity matrices. The issue is that for very small off-diagonal values (~1e-22), f32 precision causes the Householder reflection axis to not be exactly unit-sized after the initial scaling by factor.sqrt(), leading to very inaccurate singular values (e.g. 2.12 instead of 1). The patch adds a second normalization step to correct this precision loss. This is an accuracy problem due to floating-point rounding/precision loss, not a special-value, convergence, or pure-logic issue.",
            "evidence": "PR#1369: \"Fix numerical issue on SVD with near-identity matrix ... The column may not be normalized if the `factor` is on a scale of 1e-40. Possibly, `f32` just runs out of precision.\" Diff in src/linalg/householder.rs: \"Normalize again, making sure the vector is unit-sized ... the first normalization ... might end up with a slightly non-unit vector (especially when using 32-bits float).\" Issue#1368 reproduces wrong singular values for small-valued near-identity matrices."
          },
          "grounded_on": [
